# Team Git workflow — dev → V1 (preprod) → V1.0.1 (prod)

Applies to Claude Code and Cursor for every team member. When someone says a trigger word below, run that procedure step by step. On any failure, stop and report; don't improvise.

## 1. The three levels

| Level | Repo / branch | Who merges | Site | Database |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Prod** | `Vasanthgogox/Pulse-app` → `V1.0.1` | Vasanth | gogopulse.com (Netlify, auto on merge) | Prod `nafxpivddesgsrthmosv` |
| **Integration / preprod** | `nihas-gogox/Pulse-app` → `V1` | Nihas | gx-pulse.netlify.app (auto from `V1`) | Preprod `xbisiveavvbifbzyfhgy` |
| **Dev** | `<name>/V1.0.<n>` on your own fork | — | none | none (local only) |

- `V1.0.1` on Vasanth's repo is the **name of the prod branch**, not a version number. It stays `V1.0.1`.
- Dev branch numbers (`V1.0.2`, `V1.0.3`, …) count **your PRs**, one number per PR. They are not prod versions.
- Releases to prod are named by date: `release/YYYY-MM-DD`.
- Baseline (2026-10-16): prod `V1.0.1` = `389a5d3f`; `nihas-gogox` `V1` and `V1.0.1` were reset to the same commit. Older work is in tags `archive/20261016/*`.

